@startuml lifecycle
!include style.iuml
title One session across the three tiers
actor Developer as dev
participant "Agent" as ag
participant "memory/\n(git markdown)" as mb
participant "jevmem\n(hooks + MCP)" as jm
participant "AGENTS.md" as ai

== Session start ==
ai --> ag : rules (always loaded)
jm --> ag : SessionStart: pinned notes, then conventions\nand gotchas ranked by branch / commits\n(skips notes AGENTS.md already says)
ag -> mb : read activeContext.md, then progress.md
ag -> ag : stale against git log? say so and ask first

== Work ==
dev -> ag : prompt
jm --> ag : UserPromptSubmit: 0-3 on-topic notes (or nothing)
ag -> jm : memory_recall(question)\nsufficient=false -> check the code, do not guess
ag -> mb : trigger-based edits only\n(task done, focus change, blocker)

== A decision, bug cause or gotcha is settled ==
ag -> mb : decisions.md: context / decision / rationale
ag -> jm : memory_write: one dated fact + its reason\n(status-like notes are rejected)
jm -> jm : every 20 writes: supersede, dedupe,\nflag conflicts, queue promote proposals

== Hand-off ==
ag -> mb : progress checkboxes accurate,\nactiveContext names the exact next step
ag -> mb : commit with the feature (or "memory:" commit)
@enduml
